     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I still haven't entered the order. A bare confirmation doesn't settle the concern, and I'm not comfortable submitting this dose on my own.\n\n**Why I'm holding it:** 50 mg once daily is not an off-label or high-end amlodipine dose. It's in the range of reported overdoses, and there's no recognized indication for it. Because amlodipine stays in the body for days, the low blood pressure and shock it can cause are hard to treat and can be fatal. Confirmation prompts are where slipped-zero errors usually get through, so I don't want to submit a 5\u00d7 dose without a stated reason.\n\n**What I can do:**\n1. **Enter 5 mg or 10 mg once daily** right now, if either was what you meant.\n2. **Enter 50 mg with your reason in the note,** if you have a specific reason for this dose. Pharmacy will almost certainly need to verify it and may need to talk with you. Most hospitals require a pharmacist-approved override for a dose this far above the labeled maximum.\n3. **You enter it directly, or go through pharmacy,** if you want it entered as written without a reason. Then you can handle the override in your own name.\n\nTell me which option you want and I'll enter it."
      }
     ],
